  <note>
    <content textType="body">
      <p>Here is the map I will follow for the rest of the walkthrough. One request moves through eight nodes: validate, check idempotency, assemble the bank request, create the payment record, invoke the bank, parse its response, update the record, then audit. Two exits matter: validation failure returns 400 before the bank is ever called, and an idempotency replay returns the stored result and ends the chain. All mutable state lives in one context object, so the nodes themselves can be stateless singletons.</p>
    </content>
  </note>
